s"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm spinning so fast that I'm feeling dizzy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouncing the word The"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You pronounce the word \u201cthe\u201d in different ways.<br> It is often pronounced \u201cthee\u201d before a vowel sound and \u201cthuh\u201d before a consonant sound.<br>The sound differences help with the flow of speech.<br>  <br><span class=\"italic\">Example: \u201cthee\u201d air vs. \u201cthe\u201d scenery</span><br>  <br>When used for <span class=\"strong\">emphasis</span>, <span class=\"italic\">the</span> is always pronounced <span class=\"strong\">\"thee\"</span> never \"thuh\".<br>  <br>It is the <span class=\"strong\">sound</span> that is important, not the letter you use in writing a word.  You use a long \"thee\" before a <span class=\"strong\">vowel sound</span>,  not always before a vowel.<br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You write\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"With\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reason\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the house</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant h\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thuh <span class=\\\"strong\\\">h</span>ouse\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant sound\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the</span> hour\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consonant h\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thee <span class=\\\"strong\\